# NO LONGER WHAT DECIDES WHAT IS PUBLISHED, since 15 November 2026.
#
# wrangler.jsonc now points the assets directory at site/, which
# build-site.js assembles before every deploy, and wrangler reads an
# .assetsignore only from inside the assets directory. So this file is
# read by nothing. build-site.js is the allowlist: it copies what the
# site is and nothing else, and it fails closed in the same way this
# file did (a new page or asset is not served until a line there copies
# it). publish-check.sh still asks for every leak this file was written
# after, .git first.
#
# Kept, not deleted, so that if the assets directory is ever pointed
# back at the repository root, everything is hidden until somebody
# decides otherwise.

/*
